ctly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player X.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 O . .\n1 . X .\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nX(0,1), X(0,2), X(1,0), X(1,2), X(2,0), X(2,1), X(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Blocking O's potential win and setting up a winning position by occupying the center (1,1) is optimal, but center is already occupied by X; instead, the best move is to complete a diagonal or force a win—O has a winning potential at (0,0) and (2,2), so blocking (2,2) prevents O from winning. However, X already has (1,1) and (1,1) is not occupied. Wait: board shows X at (1,1). So X has (1,1). O has (0,0). Current board: (0,0)=O, (1,1)=X. To win, X needs three in a row. The center is taken. Possible win: (0,1), (1,1), (2,1) — if X plays (0,1), then X has (0,1), (1,1), (2,1). That's a column. So playing (0,1) completes a vertical line. That's a win. So X(0,1) wins immediately. Any other move doesn't guarantee a win. So best move is X(0,1).</reason>\n<answer>X(0,1)</answer>", "episode_score": 1.62, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Blocking O's potential win and setting up a winning position by occupying the center (1,1) is optimal, but center is already occupied by X; instead, the best move is to complete a diagonal or force a win—O has a winning potential at (0,0) and (2,2), so blocking (2,2) prevents O from winning. However, X already has (1,1) and (1,1) is not occupied. Wait: board shows X at (1,1). So X has (1,1). O has (0,0). Current board: (0,0)=O, (1,1)=X. To win, X needs three in a row. The center is taken. Possible win: (0,1), (1,1), (2,1) — if X plays (0,1), then X has (0,1), (1,1), (2,1). That's a column. So playing (0,1) completes a vertical line. That's a win. So X(0,1) wins immediately. Any other move doesn't guarantee a win. So best move is X(0,1).</reason>\n<answer>X(0,1)</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player O.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 O X .\n1 . X .\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nO(0,2), O(1,0), O(1,2), O(2,0), O(2,1), O(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Center and corners are key for control; O is already at (0,0), so (0,2) threatens a horizontal win and opens up corner control; (1,2) is blocked by X, so (0,2) is optimal to complete a row and create symmetry.</reason>\n<answer>O(0,2)</answer>", "episode_score": -1.8, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Center and corners are key for control; O is already at (0,0), so (0,2) threatens a horizontal win and opens up corner control; (1,2) is blocked by X, so (0,2) is optimal to complete a row and create symmetry.</reason>\n<answer>O(0,2)</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player X.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 O X O\n1 . X .\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nX(1,0), X(1,2), X(2,0), X(2,1), X(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Player X can win by placing at (2,1), completing a vertical line with the existing X at (1,1) and (0,1), forming a column of X's from top to bottom.</reason>\n<answer>X(2,1)</answer>", "episode_score": 1.0, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Player X can win by placing at (2,1), completing a vertical line with the existing X at (1,1) and (