ves:\nO(0,2), O(1,0), O(1,2), O(2,0), O(2,1), O(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Player O already has a winning position if they complete a row, column, or diagonal; currently, O is at (0,0), and X has (0,1), (1,1), so O needs to block or create a win. The center (1,1) is occupied by X, so O must aim to complete a line. The only open line for O is the top row (0,0), (0,1), (0,2) — (0,1) is X, so only (0,2) remains. Placing O at (0,2) completes the top row and wins the game.</reason>\n<answer>O(0,2)</answer>", "episode_score": -1.8, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Player O already has a winning position if they complete a row, column, or diagonal; currently, O is at (0,0), and X has (0,1), (1,1), so O needs to block or create a win. The center (1,1) is occupied by X, so O must aim to complete a line. The only open line for O is the top row (0,0), (0,1), (0,2) — (0,1) is X, so only (0,2) remains. Placing O at (0,2) completes the top row and wins the game.</reason>\n<answer>O(0,2)</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player X.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 O X O\n1 . X .\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nX(1,0), X(1,2), X(2,0), X(2,1), X(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Player X can win by placing at (2,1), completing a vertical line with the existing X at (1,1) and (0,1), forming a column of X's from top to bottom.</reason>\n<answer>X(2,1)</answer>", "episode_score": 1.0, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Player X can win by placing at (2,1), completing a vertical line with the existing X at (1,1) and (0,1), forming a column of X's from top to bottom.</reas