l point to maximize future winning opportunities</reason>\n<answer>O(0,0)</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player X.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 O . .\n1 . X .\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nX(0,1), X(0,2), X(1,0), X(1,2), X(2,0), X(2,1), X(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Blocking O's potential win on row 0 and creating a winning opportunity in column 0 by threatening a diagonal or row win</reason>\n<answer>X(0,1)</answer>", "episode_score": 1.62, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Blocking O's potential win on row 0 and creating a winning opportunity in column 0 by threatening a diagonal or row win</reason>\n<answer>X(0,1)</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player O.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 O X .\n1 . X .\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nO(0,2), O(1,0), O(1,2), O(2,0), O(2,1), O(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Blocking X's potential win on row 1 and preparing for a diagonal win; placing at (1,0) threatens a future diagonal and opens central control.</reason>\n<answer>O(1,0)</answer>", "episode_score": -1.8, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Blocking X's potential win on row 1 and preparing for a diagonal win; placing at (1,0) threatens a future diagonal and opens central control.</reason>\n<answer>O(1,0)</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player X.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 O X .\n1 O X .\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nX(0,2), X(1,2), X(2,0), X(2,1), X(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Completing the vertical column on the left (column 0) with X(2,0) would secure a win by aligning with the existing Os in rows 0 and 1, forming a vertical line of Os and Xs, but wait—no: the Os already occupy (0,0), (1,0), so that's a full column of Os. We see the pattern: X has two Os in a row in column 0 and 1, and the only way to win is to complete a line. The existing Xs are at (0,1), (1,1). So if we place X at (2,1), it completes the middle column of Xs at (0,1), (1,1), (2,1)—a vertical win. That is a winning move.</reason>\n<answer>X(2,1)</answer>", "episode_score": 1.0, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Completing the vertical column on the left (column 0) with X(2,0) would secure a win by aligning with the existing Os in rows 0 and 1, forming a vertical line of Os and Xs, but wait—no: the Os already occupy (0,0), (1,0), so that's a full column of Os. We see the pattern: X has two Os in a row in column 0 and 1, and the only way to win is to complete a line. The existing Xs are at (0,1), (1,1). So if we place X at (2,1), it completes the middle column of Xs at (0,1), (1,1), (2,1)—a vertical win. That is a winning move.</reason>\n<answer>X(2,1)</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player X.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 . . .\n1 . . .\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nX(0,0), X(0,1), X(0,2), X(1,0), X(1,1), X(1,2), X(2,0), X(2,1), X(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Center move (1,1) maximizes control and creates the most winning opportunities in all directions</reason>\n<answer>X(1,1)</answer>", "episode_score": 1.3122000000000003, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Center move (1,1) maximizes control and creates the most winning opportunities in all directions</reason>\n<answer>X(1,1)</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player O.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 . . .\n1 . X .\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nO(0,0), O(0,1), O(0,2), O(1,0), O(1,2), O(2,0), O(2,1), O(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Player X is already in the middle of the first row (1,1), and no immediate threat exists. However, O can block a potential diagonal or lateral win from X by placing at (2,0) to initiate a central control pattern, but the only viable winning move that can exploit the current structure is (0,0) to form a potential row or diagonal. Since X has a vertical gap in the middle, placing at (0,0) creates symmetry and future options. Actually, X has no immediate threat due to open space. The best move is to initiate a winning sequence with a central alignment. The only logical choice is to place at (0,0), to open a potential row and prepare for a win in the future.</reason>\n<answer>O(0,0)</answer>", "episode_score": -1.4580000000000002, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Player X is already in the middle of the first row (1,1), and no immediate threat exists. However, O can block a potential diagonal or lateral win from X by placing at (2,0) to initiate a central control pattern, but the only viable winning move that can exploit the current structure is (0,0) to form a potential row or diagonal. Since X has a vertical gap in the middle, placing at (0,0) creates symmetry and future options. Actually, X has no immediate threat due to open space. The best move is to initiate a winning sequence with a central alignment. The only logical choice is to place at (0,0), to open a potential row and prepare for a win in the future.</reason>\n<answer>O(0,0)</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player X.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 O . .\n1 . X .\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nX(0,1), X(0,2), X(1,0), X(1,2), X(2,0), X(2,1), X(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Blocking O's potential win on row 0 and creating a winning opportunity in column 0 by threatening a diagonal or row completion</reason>\n<answer>X(0,1)</answer>", "episode_score": 1.62, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Blocking O's potential win on row 0 and creating a winning opportunity in column 0 by threatening a diagonal or row completion</reason>\n<answer>X(0,1)</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player O.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 O X .\n1 . X .\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nO(0,2), O(1,0), O(1,2), O(2,0), O(2,1), O(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Completing a corner diagonal or blocking X's potential win on the main diagonal; placing at (0,2) forms a vertical win with existing O at (0,0) and threatens diagonal or horizontal completion, while also securing control over center and edge space</reason>\n<answer>O(0,2)</answer>", "episode_score": -1.8, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Completing a corner diagonal or blocking X's potential win on the main diagonal; placing at (0,2) forms a vertical win with existing O at (0,0) and threatens diagonal or horizontal completion, while also securing control over center and edge space</reason>\n<answer>O(0,2)</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player X.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 O X O\n1 . X .\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nX(1,0), X(1,2), X(2,0), X(2,1), X(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Player X can win by placing at (2,1), completing a vertical line with the existing X at (1,1) and (0,1), forming a column of X's from top to bottom.</reason>\n<answer>X(2,1)</answer>", "episode_score": 1.0, "llm