loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player X.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 . . .\n1 . X O\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nX(0,0), X(0,1), X(0,2), X(1,0), X(2,0), X(2,1), X(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Player X can win by placing at (0,0), completing a diagonal from (0,0) to (1,1) to (2,2) with X's now at (1,1), (2,2), and (0,0)</reason>\n<answer>X(0,0)</answer>", "episode_score": 0.6561, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Player X can win by placing at (0,0), completing a diagonal from (0,0) to (1,1) to (2,2) with X's now at (1,1), (2,2), and (0,0)</reason>\n<answer>X(0,0)</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player O.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 X . .\n1 . X O\n2 . . .\n\nLegal moves:\nO(0,1), O(0,2), O(1,0), O(2,0), O(2,1), O(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>PlayerXis already winning a row in the first column (0,0)-(1,1)-(2,2), but not in the column; to stop potential O wins and counter O in the middle, O must block where it’s needed to form threat to a row or column. O already occupies the center of middle row, and if not, a win possible in center column or middle row. O can expand in middle row or column; O's presence in (1,2) means the 3rd column is already blocked, but (1,0) fills the empty space in row 1 where no X exists in column, but X already occupies column 0 in 1st row and column 1 of middle. The open move is at O(2,1), to secure middle column and block the possibility of X winning. So the most effective move in blocking the opponent’s future win and creating a path to win is to occupy middle column. </reason>\n<answer>O(2,1)</answer>", "episode_score": -0.7290000000000001, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>PlayerXis already winning a row in the first column (0,0)-(1,1)-(2,2), but not in the column; to stop potential O wins and counter O in the middle, O must block where it’s needed to form threat to a row or column. O already occupies the center of middle row, and if not, a win possible in center column or middle row. O can expand in middle row or column; O's presence in (1,2) means the 3rd column is already blocked, but (1,0) fills the empty space in row 1 where no X exists in column, but X already occupies column 0 in 1st row and column 1 of middle. The open move is at O(2,1), to secure middle column and block the possibility of X winning. So the most effective move in blocking the opponent’s future win and creating a path to win is to occupy middle column. </reason>\n<answer>O(2,1)</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Tic-Tac-Toe.user\nChoose exactly one legal move that maximizes your final game outcome:\nwin is better than draw, and draw is better than loss.\n\nAnalyze the strategy as concisely as possible and choose exactly one legal action.\nDo not enumerate every legal move or the complete game tree.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>one brief reason</reason>\n<answer><SYMBOL(row,column)></answer>\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nYou are player X.\n\nBoard:\n  0 1 2\n0 X . .\n1 . X O\n2 . O .\n\nLegal moves:\nX(0,1), X(0,2), X(1,0), X(2,0), X(2,2)assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Blocking O's potential win on row 2 and creating a winning opportunity in column 0 by threatening a diagonal or row completion</reason>\n<answer>X(0,2)</answer>", "episode_score": 0.6200000000000001, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Blocking O's potential win on row 2 and 